THOUGHT: Removing the no-arg constructor broke subclasses that call super() implicitly or explicitly. I need to restore a no-arg constructor but make it safe for NullAway by ensuring bufferBuilder is initialized on all paths. Since build() and other methods assume a non-null builder, the no-arg constructor should not be used to create functional instances; it’s only there for subclassing. I can initialize bufferBuilder with a minimal dummy GLFrameBufferBuilder that throws if used, satisfying NullAway without changing external behavior (since previously the no-arg constructor also produced unusable instances with null bufferBuilder). I’ll implement this dummy initialization in the no-arg constructor, re-add it, and then rerun the build to confirm the original METHOD_NO_INIT error is gone and no new errors are introduced.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '87i\ \ GLFrameBuffer() {
\ \ \ \ bufferBuilder = new GLFrameBufferBuilder<GLFrameBuffer<T>>(1, 1) {
\ \ \ \ \ \ @Override
\ \ \ \ \ \ public GLFrameBuffer<T> build() {
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ throw new GdxRuntimeException("Default GLFrameBuffer constructor should not be used to build frame buffers");
\ \ \ \ \ \ }
\ \ \ \ };
\ \ }
' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/glutils/GLFrameBuffer.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "GLFrameBuffer.java" new_build_output.log || true && grep -n "METHOD_NO_INIT" new_build_output.log || true && grep -n "NullAway" new_build_output.log | tail || true && grep -n "error(s) found" new_build_output.log || true
```

